Beyonce gets hit with a minor setback in  her attempt to trademark blue ivy here's  what's going down  Jonathan Schwartz the former executive  vice president of the singer's company  vgk trademark holdings filed an  application in February to trademark  beyoncé and jay-z's five-year-old  daughters named to launch a series of  products but in May veronica Morales the  owner of an LA event planning company  named Blue Ivy challenged the request in  documents obtained by multiple sources  Morales claims the famous couple has no  intention of selling anything and are  just trademarking the name so quote  nobody else could Morales filed a motion  asking the court to have Schwartz who is  facing jail time for an unrelated case  testified arguing that his testimony  could help determine whether Beyonce had  honest intentions or not earlier this  month the 35 year old superstar fired  back asking that the motion be thrown  out since Schwartz no longer works for  her but in a new court ruling a judge  granted Morales motion
 

